This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

**Session 1 (completed):** Five UI cleanup tasks for the AuraVault app:
- Remove Grafana card/section from center detail view entirely
- Remove artwork gallery images that appear above the table in room detail (artworks only in table)
- Fix X-axis of historical charts to show real timestamps: 1h→HH:MM:SS/10min/max8, 12h→HH:MM/1h/max12, 24h→HH:MM/2h/max12; never numeric indices; rotate 45° if needed
- Check all Artwork image URLs in Orion, fix broken ones using Wikipedia/Wikimedia Commons/official museums
- Apply consistent glassmorphism across the entire app in a single global CSS file with dark gradient background, decorative blobs, backdrop-filter on all cards/modals/navbar/buttons; dark mode intensifies, light mode softens

**Session 2 (in progress):** Four more tasks:
- Change light mode to a lighter green (verde claro) since current dark background causes readability issues
- Definitively eliminate Grafana panel from center detail view (verify fully gone)
- Find congruent real images for each of the 24 rooms in Orion (preferably from the actual centers), and fix artwork images that don't load correctly
- Add symbols/emojis next to material and technique values in the artwork table

Both sessions end with: commit, push, and update PRD.md, architecture.md, data_model.md.

---

2. Key Technical Concepts:

- **AuraVault**: FIWARE/NGSI-LD platform for environmental monitoring of cultural spaces (MUNCYT, Bellas Artes, Teatro Rosalía, Palacio de la Ópera — all in A Coruña)
- **Orion Context Broker**: NGSI-LD at `http://localhost:1026`, entities queried via `/ngsi-ld/v1/entities?type=X`
- **NGSI-LD PATCH**: `PATCH /ngsi-ld/v1/entities/{encoded_id}/attrs` with `Content-Type: application/json`
- **Flask + Flask-SocketIO**: Backend on port 5000; WebSocket updates every 30s
- **Chart.js 4.4.3**: Used for historical charts; `ticks.callback` formats X-axis labels; `maxTicksLimit` controls density
- **CSS Glassmorphism**: `backdrop-filter: blur()`, `rgba()` transparent backgrounds, `border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.x)`
- **CSS Variables**: `:root` for light mode, `[data-theme="dark"]` for dark mode
- **MediaWiki API**: `https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&titles=File:NAME&prop=imageinfo&iiprop=url&iiurlwidth=800&format=json` to get direct `upload.wikimedia.org` thumbnail URLs
- **Wikimedia Special:FilePath**: Rate-limited by Wikimedia (429) when accessed programmatically; must use direct `upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/...` URLs instead
- **CERES Museum URLs**: `https://ceres.mcu.es/pages/Viewer?img=...` returns `image/jpeg` directly (verified)
- **Room entities**: 24 total rooms across 4 centers, all with `NO_IMAGE` or placeholder
- **Artwork entities**: 24 total; 17 updated to direct Wikimedia URLs; 7 use CERES (verified working)
- **Branch**: `feature/issue-17-ui-artwork-cleanup`

---

3. Files and Code Sections:

- **`backend/templates/center_detail.html`**
  - Removed entire Grafana article block (was lines 100-108):
    ```html
    <article class="card">
        <h3 data-i18n="grafana">Grafana — Monitorización avanzada</h3>
        <div id="grafanaError" class="empty-state" style="display:none;margin-bottom:8px">
            <p>⚠️ El panel de Grafana no está disponible...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grafana-frame" id="grafanaContainer">
            <iframe id="grafanaFrame" title="Grafana center" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div>
    </article>
    ```

- **`backend/static/js/center_detail.js`**
  - Removed `loadGrafana(code)` function entirely
  - Removed `loadGrafana(code)` from `bootCenterDetail()` Promise.all array
  - Current `bootCenterDetail`:
    ```js
    async function bootCenterDetail() {
      const code = centerCodeFromPath();
      await Promise.all([
        loadCenterSnapshot(code),
        loadRooms(code),
        loadRiskArtworks(code),
        loadHistory(code),
        loadActuators(code),
      ]);
      ...
    }
    ```

- **`backend/templates/room_artwork.html`**
  - Removed gallery div: `<div class="gallery-container" id="artworksGallery" aria-label="Galería de obras">` and its contents

- **`backend/static/js/room_artwork.js`**
  - Removed `renderGallery(artworks)` call from `loadRoomView()`
  - Added `buildXAxisConfig(range, labels)` function:
    ```js
    function buildXAxisConfig(range, labels) {
      let maxTicksLimit, useSeconds;
      if (range === '1h') { maxTicksLimit = 8; useSeconds = true; }
      else if (range === '12h') { maxTicksLimit = 12; useSeconds = false; }
      else { maxTicksLimit = 12; useSeconds = false; }
      return {
        ticks: {
          maxRotation: 45, minRotation: 0, autoSkip: true, maxTicksLimit,
          font: { size: 10 },
          callback: function(val, index) {
            const ts = labels[index];
            if (!ts) return '';
            try {
              const d = new Date(ts);
              if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return '';
              if (useSeconds) return d.toLocaleTimeString('es-ES', { hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', second: '2-digit' });
              return d.toLocaleTimeString('es-ES', { hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit' });
            } catch { return ''; }
          }
        },
        grid: { display: false }
      };
    }
    ```
  - `renderIndividualCharts(history, range)` now accepts range and uses `buildXAxisConfig`
  - `changeRange(range)` calls `renderIndividualCharts(history || {}, range)`
  - Initial load calls `renderIndividualCharts(history || {}, currentRange)`

- **`backend/static/css/style.css`** — Major file (~1200+ lines)
  - **Session 1 changes (completed):**
    - `:root` changed to dark base: `--bg: #162422`, `--text: #eef3f0`, `--muted: #9dbdb8`, `--accent: #45c5bb`, `--border: rgba(255,255,255,0.18)`, `--radius: 16px`
    - `[data-theme="dark"]`: `--bg: #060e0d`, `--panel: rgba(255,255,255,0.05)`
    - `body::before/after` decorative blobs with `filter: blur(90px)`
    - Body: dark gradient with 3 radial-gradient color blobs
    - `.card`: `background: var(--panel)`, `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)`, `border: 1px solid var(--border)`
    - `.topbar`: `background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12)`, `backdrop-filter: blur(18px)`
    - `.btn`: `background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12)`, `border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.25)`, `backdrop-filter: blur(8px)`
    - All `color-mix()` on rgba variables replaced with direct rgba values
    - `.artwork-zoom-content`, `.modal-content`, `.timeline-item`, `.alert-item`, `.chart-item` all glass-styled
    - Dark mode overrides for `.topbar`, `.btn`, `.artwork-zoom-content`, `.modal-content`
    - `.hero-card` updated for dark background
    - `select option { background: #1c2e2c; }` for dark dropdown
  - **Session 2 changes (IN PROGRESS — partially done):**
    - `:root` and `[data-theme="dark"]` blocks completely rewritten to add glass CSS variable system:
    ```css
    :root {
      --bg: #c4ddd8;           /* light sage-green */
      --panel: rgba(255,255,255,0.62);
      --text: #182e2b;          /* dark text */
      --muted: #4a7a74;
      --accent: #0e7c74;
      --accent-2: #c05e1e;
      --danger: #b5443c;
      --warn: #a86b18;
      --ok: #1d7048;
      --border: rgba(0,0,0,0.13);
      --shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.10);
      --radius: 16px;
      /* Glass system — light */
      --glass-bg:     rgba(255,255,255,0.62);
      --glass-sm:     rgba(255,255,255,0.46);
      --glass-border: rgba(0,0,0,0.13);
      --glass-topbar: rgba(255,255,255,0.74);
      --glass-btn:    rgba(255,255,255,0.62);
      --glass-btn-h:  rgba(255,255,255,0.86);
      --glass-input:  rgba(255,255,255,0.62);
      --glass-chart:  rgba(255,255,255,0.38);
      --glass-modal:  rgba(255,255,255,0.72);
      --blob-1:       rgba(14,124,116,0.22);
      --blob-2:       rgba(210,125,63,0.16);
    }
    [data-theme="dark"] {
      --bg: #060e0d;
      --panel: rgba(255,255,255,0.07);
      --text: #e4ecea; --muted: #7a9e98; --accent: #45c5bb; --accent-2: #f0a15d;
      --danger: #ea7164; --warn: #f0bb62; --ok: #51d494;
      --border: rgba(255,255,255,0.09);
      --shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);
      /* Glass system — dark */
      --glass-bg:     rgba(255,255,255,0.07);
      --glass-sm:     rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
      --glass-border: rgba(255,255,255,0.09);
      --glass-topbar: rgba(0,0,0,0.28);
      --glass-btn:    rgba(255,255,255,0.07);
      --glass-btn-h:  rgba(255,255,255,0.14);
      --glass-input:  rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      --glass-chart:  rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      --glass-modal:  rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      --blob-1:       rgba(69,197,187,0.16);
      --blob-2:       rgba(240,161,93,0.14);
    }
    ```
    - This edit was completed. The next steps (updating body, blobs, topbar, btn, etc. to use the new variables) have NOT yet been done.

- **`PRD.md`**, **`architecture.md`**, **`data_model.md`** — Updated with Session 1 implementation notes (glassmorphism, Grafana removal, image fixes, X-axis correction)

---

4. Errors and Fixes:

- **Wikimedia 429 Rate Limiting**: `Special:FilePath` URLs returned HTTP 429 when accessed rapidly in a loop. Fix: Used the MediaWiki API (`commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&prop=imageinfo&iiurlwidth=800`) with delays to get direct `upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/...` URLs, then PATCHed Orion. All 8 broken + 9 additional artworks updated.

- **Subagent blocked by permissions**: A background agent launched to check Orion image URLs was blocked by the permissions system (couldn't run Bash/curl). Fix: The main agent (Claude) handled the task directly using the Bash tool with Python3 urllib.

- **`color-mix()` with rgba variables**: After changing `--panel` and `--border` to rgba values, existing `color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 70%, transparent)` calls became unreliable. Fix: Replaced all such calls with direct `rgba(255,255,255,x)` values throughout style.css.

- **select option visibility**: Native `<select>` dropdowns were invisible against dark background. Fix: Added `select option { background: #1c2e2c; color: var(--text); }`.

---

5. Problem Solving:

**Session 1 (resolved):**
- Grafana card removed cleanly from both HTML and JS
- Gallery duplication above table eliminated; artworks only in table
- X-axis formatting uses real timestamps via `ticks.callback` keyed by range
- Artwork images: 17/24 migrated from `Special:FilePath` to direct upload.wikimedia.org URLs; 7 CERES URLs verified as `image/jpeg`
- Glassmorphism applied globally: dark gradient body, glass cards/navbar/modals/buttons; dark mode intensifies blur; light mode more opaque

**Session 2 (in progress):**
- Rooms: all 24 have NO_IMAGE — need to find real congruent images for each
- Light mode: currently dark (#162422 bg) causing readability issues → being changed to light green (#c4ddd8) with dark text and new glass variable system
- Glass variable system introduced but element styles not yet updated to use the new variables

---

6. All User Messages:

**Message 1:** "Revisa PRD.md, architecture.md y data_model.md antes de empezar. [5 tasks with screenshots: 1.ELIMINAR TARJETA GRAFANA 2.ELIMINAR IMÁGENES SOBRE LA TABLA EN DETALLE DE SALA 3.EJE X DE GRÁFICAS HISTÓRICAS EN DETALLE DE SALA 4.IMÁGENES DE OBRAS 5.GLASSMORPHISM EN TODA LA WEB] Haz commit y push al finalizar y actualiza PRD.md, architecture.md y data_model.md."

**Message 2:** "Revisa PRD.md, architecture.md y data_model.md antes de empezar. - Modifica el color del estilo de la pagina del modo claro a uno más claro (verde claro) ya que no permite ver bien algunas cosas. - Que elimine definitivamente el panel de grafana de la vista detalle de cada centro. - Que para cada sala de cada centro busque en internet una imagen congruente y distintas unas de otras que representen una sala de un museo, teatro o lo que sea que representan (a poder ser del centro que estan representando). Lo mismo para aquellas obras cuyas imagenes no se cargan correctamente. - En la tabla de obras en material poner al lado del atributo un simbolo que lo represente como por ejemplo costumbrismo, etc. Haz commit y push al finalizar y actualiza PRD.md, architecture.md y data_model.md."

---

7. Pending Tasks:

From Session 2 (all pending):
1. **Complete the light mode CSS update**: After the `:root`/`[data-theme="dark"]` variable edit, need to update all hardcoded `rgba(255,255,255,...)` values in the CSS to use the new `var(--glass-bg)`, `var(--glass-topbar)`, `var(--glass-btn)`, `var(--glass-border)`, `var(--glass-sm)`, `var(--glass-input)`, `var(--glass-chart)`, `var(--glass-modal)`, `var(--blob-1)`, `var(--blob-2)` variables; update body background gradient for light mode; update `body::before`/`after` blobs to use `var(--blob-1)`/`var(--blob-2)`
2. **Verify Grafana is definitively gone** from center_detail (already done in Session 1 but user asked again — may need to double-check no JS references remain)
3. **Find and assign room images**: For all 24 rooms (MUNCYT: muncyt-creadores, muncyt-ex-catedra, muncyt-miscelanea, muncyt-piezas-con-memoria, muncyt-salon-de-actos, muncyt-temporales; Bellas Artes: bellasartes-goya, bellasartes-sargadelos, bellasartes-siglo-xx, bellasartes-siglos-xvi-xvii, bellasartes-siglos-xviii-xix, bellasartes-temporales; Teatro Rosalía: rosalia-anfiteatro, rosalia-camerinos, rosalia-escenario, rosalia-foyer, rosalia-palcos, rosalia-patio-butacas; Palacio de la Ópera: opera-auditorio-principal, opera-hall-camara, opera-sala-crescendo, opera-sala-sonata, opera-sala-vivace, opera-salon-wengue) — find congruent, distinct, real images from the internet (preferably from the actual centers) and PATCH Orion
4. **Fix remaining broken artwork images** (any that don't load correctly after Session 1 fixes)
5. **Add material/technique symbols** in the artwork table in `room_artwork.js` `renderArtworkTable` function (emoji/icon next to material and technique tags, e.g., 🎨 for painting, 🪨 for sculpture, etc.)
6. **Commit, push, and update PRD.md, architecture.md, data_model.md** with all changes

---

8. Current Work:

Immediately before the summary request, the assistant was working on **Task 1 of Session 2: changing light mode to verde claro**. The assistant had just completed one edit to `backend/static/css/style.css`:

The `:root` and `[data-theme="dark"]` blocks were rewritten to:
- Change `--bg` from `#162422` (dark) to `#c4ddd8` (light sage-green)
- Change `--text` from `#eef3f0` (light) to `#182e2b` (dark, for readability on light background)
- Change `--muted` from `#9dbdb8` to `#4a7a74`
- Change `--accent` from `#45c5bb` to `#0e7c74` (darker for light bg)
- Change `--accent-2` from `#f0a15d` to `#c05e1e`
- Change `--border` from `rgba(255,255,255,0.18)` to `rgba(0,0,0,0.13)`
- Introduce 11 new CSS glass variables: `--glass-bg`, `--glass-sm`, `--glass-border`, `--glass-topbar`, `--glass-btn`, `--glass-btn-h`, `--glass-input`, `--glass-chart`, `--glass-modal`, `--blob-1`, `--blob-2` — with appropriate values for both light (`:root`) and dark (`[data-theme="dark"]`) modes.

This edit was completed successfully. The remaining edits needed to complete the light mode change are:
- Update `body::before` to use `var(--blob-1)` instead of hardcoded `rgba(69,197,187,0.2)`
- Update `body::after` to use `var(--blob-2)`
- Update `body` background gradient for the new light green base
- Update `.topbar` to use `var(--glass-topbar)` and `var(--glass-border)`
- Remove or update `[data-theme="dark"] .topbar` (now handled by variables)
- Update `.btn` to use `var(--glass-btn)` and `var(--glass-border)`
- Update `.btn:hover` to use `var(--glass-btn-h)`
- Remove `[data-theme="dark"] .btn` and `[data-theme="dark"] .btn:hover` overrides
- Update `.nav-link.active, .nav-link:hover` to use `var(--glass-sm)` and `var(--glass-border)`
- Update `.alert-item`, `.timeline-item`, `.chart-wrap` etc. to use glass variables
- Update `.artwork-zoom-content`, `.modal-content` to use `var(--glass-modal)`
- Update `.mini-metric`, `.attribute-group`, `.risk-progress` etc.
- Update `select option` background for light mode

---

9. Optional Next Step:

Continue updating `backend/static/css/style.css` to use the new CSS glass variables introduced in the `:root` and `[data-theme="dark"]` blocks. The user asked: "Modifica el color del estilo de la pagina del modo claro a uno más claro (verde claro) ya que no permite ver bien algunas cosas."

The next immediate edit should update the body blobs and body background gradient, then the topbar, buttons, and nav-links:

```css
/* Update body::before */
body::before { background: var(--blob-1); }
body::after { background: var(--blob-2); }

/* Update body background for light mode */
body {
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 12% 20%, rgba(14,124,116,0.18) 0, transparent 48%),
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 88% 8%, rgba(210,125,63,0.14) 0, transparent 45%),
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 52% 88%, rgba(60,140,100,0.12) 0, transparent 42%),
    linear-gradient(145deg, var(--bg) 0%, #aecfc8 100%);
}

/* Update .topbar */
.topbar { background: var(--glass-topbar); border-color: var(--glass-border); }

/* Remove dark-specific topbar override (now handled by variables) */
/* Update .btn */
.btn { background: var(--glass-btn); border-color: var(--glass-border); }
.btn:hover { background: var(--glass-btn-h); }
```

This is directly in line with the user's request: "Modifica el color del estilo de la pagina del modo claro a uno más claro (verde claro) ya que no permite ver bien algunas cosas."

If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/hugobaladomosquera/.claude/projects/-Users-hugobaladomosquera-Cuarto-GDEI-Pr-cticas-GDEI-P3/19b4193e-c2d6-4332-aae0-6b2d5584f20c.jsonl
Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with "I'll continue" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.

